## Architectural Strategy

The FinOps architecture combines declarative infrastructure as code with serverless event orchestration:

1. **Tag-Driven Lifecycle Enforcement**: Cloud resources tagged with environment tiers (`staging`, `sandbox`, `preview`) register with an automated state machine.
1. **Scheduled Teardown via Serverless Cron**: AWS EventBridge rules trigger Python Lambda handlers to gracefully spin down non-critical services outside active sprint hours.
1. **Auto-Scaling Rightsizing**: Dynamic scaling thresholds replace static instance sizing, adapting task capacities based on actual memory and CPU telemetry gathered through Amazon CloudWatch.

> **KEY OPERATING PRINCIPLE**
> 
> Automation must never surprise developers. All shutdown events dispatch Slack notifications 15 minutes before execution, providing single-click webhook overrides when developers require extended test sessions.

## Declarative Standardization with Terraform & CDK

All target workloads were migrated to reusable Terraform modules and AWS CDK constructs. By defining consistent tagging schemas (`Environment`, `CostCenter`, `Owner`), financial allocation became transparent across engineering teams.
